// Find a row in a BigQuery table.
// Limitation: the bigquery adaptor only exposes load() (bulk-load local files into a table);
// it has no query function, and the credential is a service-account key, so there's no
// access token to call the REST API with fn(). To run SQL, use a separate step with the
// http adaptor (OAuth access token) against POST /projects/{projectId}/queries:
//
// post(`https://bigquery.googleapis.com/bigquery/v2/projects/${$.configuration.project_id}/queries`, {
//   query: `SELECT * FROM my_dataset.beneficiaries WHERE national_id = '${$.data.nationalId}' LIMIT 1`,
//   useLegacySql: false,
// });
//
// Results come back as rows of { f: [{ v }] } cells, in the order of schema.fields.

